1      Introduction
1.1     Background
    Tennis matches are exciting and ever-changing. Players who seem to be dominating expe-
rience incredible swings from time to time. For example, a player may be in control of the
match with a series of points, but at one rally, the opponent suddenly breaks and the situation is




                                                                                型
reversed. We often attribute this dramatic turn of events to "momentum".
    "Momentum" heightens emotional intensity in the match, creating unpredictability and




                                                                模
anticipation, making each moment charged and intense.




                                                               学
                                                      数
                                     ：

