5.2.1    Impact of Short-term Motivation and Confidence Boost on Serve Success Rate
    Short-term Motivation refers to a brief period of above-average performance by a player
following a motivating event (e.g., a breaking serve) during a match, a phenomenon known
in sports as "hot hands"[1]. We developed a probabilistic model that quantifies Short-term
Motivation as an increase in serve success rate.
    The following two assumptions are necessary:
